{"id": "185128", "name": "a.iii composition (paths as graphs)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "functions": [{"name": "x1", "params": ["t"], "body": "x1"}, {"name": "y1", "params": ["t"], "body": "y1"}, {"name": "x2", "params": ["t"], "body": "x2"}, {"name": "y2", "params": ["t"], "body": "y2"}, {"name": "x3", "params": ["t"], "body": "x3"}, {"name": "y3", "params": ["t"], "body": "y3"}], "questiontext": "<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Let \\(f(x,y)={{CT:0}}\\)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Consider three functions \\(\\alpha_i: [a,b] \\rightarrow R^2\\) from an interval inside the real line to the plane. The resulting paths in the plane are depicted below. </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>Each function \\(g_i = f \\circ \\alpha_i: [a,b] \\rightarrow R\\) is a composition of \\(f(x,y)\\) with one of these paths. Match each function with the graph of the corresponding path.</p>\n<p>(Please answer with 1, 2 or 3)</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(g_1(t)={{CT:1}}\\)</p>\n<p>Path number: [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(g_2(t)={{CT:2}}\\)</p>\n<p>Path number: [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p>\\(g_3(t)={{CT:3}}\\)</p>\n<p>Path number: [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">path 1</span>:</p>\n<p><span>{{CT:4}}</span></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">path 2</span>:</p>\n<p>{{CT:5}}</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">path 3</span>:</p>\n<p>{{CT:6}}</p>\n<p> </p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>\n<p> </p>\n<p><br /><br /></p>\n<p> </p>", "generalfeedback": "", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]<br />[[feedback:prt2]]<br />[[feedback:prt3]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p>Correct answer, well done.</p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p>Your answer is partially correct.</p>", "prtincorrect": "<p>Incorrect answer.</p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans2", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}, {"name": "ans3", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 5, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": ""}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "sol1", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-T", "feedback": "<p>The first match is correct.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt1-1-F", "feedback": "<p>The first match is incorrect, {{CT:7}} is the correct path.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt2", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans2", "tans": "sol2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-T", "feedback": "<p>The second match is correct.</p>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "+", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "prt2-1-F", "feedback": "<p>The second match is incorrect, {{CT:8}} is the correct path.</p>"}}]}, {"name": "prt3", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans3", "t